### Files created

1. **`ros2_stack/scripts/setup_mower.sh`** — Idempotent mower setup script with:
   - `set -euo pipefail`
   - OS detection (expects Ubuntu 20.04 aarch64, warns on mismatch)
   - Free disk space check on `/` (warns if <10 GB)
   - Installs `docker.io` via `apt` (sudo guard — refuses to run non-root without sudo)
   - Adds current user to the `docker` group
   - iptables/nft caveat
   - Verifies Docker with `docker info` (not `docker run hello-world`, which doesn't work off-image)
   - Optional pre-pull of `ros:humble-ros-base-jammy` via `PRE_PULL=1`

2. **`ros2_stack/scripts/preflight.sh`** — Preflight checks with:
   - Docker presence check
   - Serial device node symlink verification (`/dev/serial_mower` → `ttyS9`, `/dev/serial_imu` → `ttyS1`, `/dev/serial_rtk` → `ttyS4`)
   - Vendor service check (`systemctl is-active mower-base`/`mower-logic`/`mower-controller`, warns if active)
   - `/userdata` free disk check (warns if <10 GB)
   - Go/no-go summary printout

3. **`ros2_stack/docs/deployment.md`** — Added 'Mower-side setup' section (lines 59–70) referencing both scripts, with `chmod +x` reminder.

Both scripts use English comments, `set -euo pipefail`, and sudo guards where needed.
